
   {
    "name": "Decks and Outdoor Living",
    "description": [
     "What Makes Deck and Outdoor Living Clients Unique: Outdoor living clients view their backyard as an essential extension of their home's square footage, tailored for year-round coastal entertaining and relaxation. In the Lowcountry, outdoor spaces face continuous sun exposure, high humidity, salt air, and insects. Clients demand low-maintenance deck materials, structural integrity against tropical weather, screen enclosures that maintain clear sightlines, and cohesive transitions between indoors and outdoors. They require a builder who understands local code setback limits, soil bearing capacities, HOA architectural board guidelines, and precise carpentry framing.",
     "Material: GEA Construction utilizes high-performance composite decking (Trex, TimberTech, Fiberon), pressure-treated structural pine framing, stainless steel structural hardware, hidden deck fasteners, powder-coated aluminum railing systems, and heavy-duty mesh screening.",
     "Installation Process Overview: Our process begins with site layout and digging concrete footings below frost lines to meet local building codes. GEA Construction sets post anchors, constructs pressure-treated support joist framing, installs composite decking boards using hidden fastener clips for a screw-free surface, secures aluminum or cable railings, and constructs custom screen superstructures or timber pergolas.",
     "Timing: A custom composite deck or screened porch build is completed within 1 to 2 weeks, depending on structural size, roofline integration, and soil footing requirements.",
     "Customization: Custom outdoor living options include multi-level deck designs, picture-frame board borders, built-in bench seating, integrated LED stair riser lights, cocktail railing tops, screened porches with vaulted ceilings, and under-deck drainage systems.",
     "Maintenance: Composite decking and aluminum railing systems eliminate the constant staining, sanding, and sealing cycles required by natural wood. Simple washing with a soft hose, mild soap, and a soft brush clears pine straw tannins and coastal sand.",
     "Benefits: Custom composite decks and screened porches installed by GEA Construction expand usable living space without rotting, splintering, or twisting under extreme South Carolina humidity, providing a safe, bug-free outdoor sanctuary.",
     "Value: Custom outdoor living structures represent one of the most desired upgrades in coastal real estate markets. Composite decks and screened porches dramatically expand functional home square footage, yielding exceptional equity retention.",
     "Residential Service Areas and Regional Infrastructure: GEA Construction builds custom decks, screen porches, and outdoor living structures across Beaufort and Jasper counties. Our service areas include Beaufort, Bluffton, Hardeeville, Hilton Head, Okatie, and Ridgeland. GEA Construction manages all engineering permits and HOA submittals directly."
    ],
