   {
    "name": "Patios and Hardscaping",
    "description": [
     "What Makes Patio and Hardscaping Clients Unique: Hardscaping clients seek to transform muddy, uneven, or underutilized backyard yards into beautiful, functional, and permanent stone entertaining spaces. Coastal backyards frequently suffer from standing water, soil erosion, and intense heat that degrades natural turf. Hardscaping clients prioritize structural base preparation, long-term level stability, effective drainage integration, and rich stone textures that complement their home's exterior architecture. They need a hardscaping contractor who executes correct soil excavation, uses heavy compaction machinery, and understands proper joint sanding techniques.",
     "Material: GEA Construction utilizes high-density architectural concrete pavers, natural travertine, slate, granite, modular retaining wall units, crushed aggregate sub-bases, and polymeric joint sand systems engineered for coastal rainwater exposure.",
     "Installation Process Overview: Precision hardscaping relies on meticulous ground preparation. GEA Construction excavates subsoil to specified depths, lays crushed stone aggregate base material, compacts the base to maximum density with mechanical plate compactors, screeds bedding sand, lays pavers in custom geometric patterns, secures heavy-duty edge restraints, and vibrates polymeric sand into joints to lock blocks in place.",
     "Timing: Most residential paver patio, fire pit, and walkway installations are executed within 3 to 5 business days, allowing immediate outdoor use upon joint sand curing.",
     "Customization: Customization options include custom paver laying patterns (herringbone, ashlar slate, running bond), contrasting soldier course borders, raised fire pit zones, built-in seat walls, natural travertine pool deck surrounds, and integrated landscape lighting.",
     "Maintenance: GEA Construction hardscapes are durable and low-maintenance. Locked polymeric sand joints stop weed germination and insect burrowing, while non-porous paver surfaces allow quick rinsing with a garden hose or pressure washer.",
     "Benefits: Custom paver patios from GEA Construction eliminate mud tracking into the house, eliminate turf maintenance in shade zones, fix standing rainwater puddle issues through sub-grade pitching, and offer superior heat resistance.",
     "Value: Professionally built hardscape patios extend functional outdoor dining and cooking square footage. High-end stone hardscaping boosts overall property curb appeal and delivers immediate value retention in Lowcountry neighborhoods.",
     "Residential Service Areas and Regional Infrastructure: GEA Construction delivers paver patio construction and custom hardscaping across the Lowcountry. Our core service areas include Beaufort, Bluffton, Hardeeville, Hilton Head, Okatie, and Ridgeland. GEA Construction operates heavy compaction equipment and maintains direct sourcing for regional pavers."
    ],
